IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nsw-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `nsw-p3-commencement`
IMPORT `nsw-p4-repeals`
IMPORT `nsw-p5-construction`
IMPORT `nsw-p6-statutory-rules`
IMPORT `nsw-p11-misc`
IMPORT `nsw-definitions`

-- Interpretation Act 1987 (New South Wales), No 15 of 1987 -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: a person who has a time limit to meet under a New South Wales Act or statutory rule (to apply, object, appeal, reply or pay), or who needs to know when something takes effect, asking on which day their period ends and which of their days count.
--
-- This layer asks the questions that person would ask and calls the layer-1 rules to answer them. Nothing here is new law.
-- Every question takes plain inputs, one for each fact the person can state, and every @desc is worded as the person would be asked.
-- Where the Act hands a judgment or a borrowed fact to someone else (which days are public holidays in the place, which days a House of Parliament sat), the answer is asked as an input and never guessed.
-- A question the Act does not answer returns NOTHING, which the website shows as "the Act does not say".
-- The text does not define "day", "week" or "year", so a period counted in weeks or years returns NOTHING (a period in calendar years counts only from 1 January).
-- The first day of a period counted from a day or an event is the next day (section 36(1)); a month is a calendar month (Schedule 4).

§ `Interpretation Act 1987 (NSW) -- the questions of a person with a time limit`

§§ `Counting a period of time (section 36 and Schedule 4)`

-- s 36(1) and Schedule 4. "If in any Act or instrument a period of time, dating from a given day, act or event, is prescribed or allowed for any purpose, the time shall be reckoned exclusive of that day". The last day of a period of N days is the Nth day after the given day. A period of months is a number of successive calendar months, the first beginning the day after the given day.
@export On which day does my period end (s 36(1), Schedule 4)?
GIVEN `the day my period dates from` IS A DATE @desc On which day did the act or event happen from which your period runs? (for example, the day you were given the notice)
      `the unit of my period` IS A PeriodUnit @desc Is your period counted in days, weeks, months, years or calendar years? (choose PeriodOfDays, PeriodOfWeeks, PeriodOfMonths, PeriodOfYears or PeriodOfCalendarYears)
      `the number of units in my period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of those units does your period run for?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On which day does my period end` IS
    `s 36 the last day of a period of n units dating from a given day` `the day my period dates from` `the unit of my period` `the number of units in my period`

-- s 36(2). If the last day of a period prescribed or allowed for doing a thing falls on a Saturday or Sunday, or on a public holiday or bank holiday in the place where the thing is to be done, the thing may be done on the first day following that is not a Saturday, a Sunday or such a holiday.
@export By which day must I act, allowing for weekends and holidays (s 36(1), s 36(2))?
GIVEN `the day my period dates from` IS A DATE @desc On which day did the act or event happen from which your period runs?
      `the unit of my period` IS A PeriodUnit @desc Is your period counted in days, weeks, months, years or calendar years? (choose PeriodOfDays, PeriodOfWeeks, PeriodOfMonths, PeriodOfYears or PeriodOfCalendarYears)
      `the number of units in my period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of those units does your period run for?
      `the public and bank holidays in the place where I must act` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc Which days in or near your period are public holidays or bank holidays in the place where the thing is to be done? (list each day)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `By which day must I act` IS
    `s 36 the latest day on which a thing may be done within a period of n units dating from a given day` `the day my period dates from` `the unit of my period` `the number of units in my period` `the public and bank holidays in the place where I must act`

-- s 36(1). The day itself is not counted; the last day is counted.
@export Is the day I am asking about inside my period of days (s 36(1))?
GIVEN `the day my period dates from` IS A DATE @desc On which day did the act or event happen from which your period runs?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which day do you want to know about?
      `the number of days in my period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days does your period run for?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the day I am asking about inside my period of days` IS
    `s 36(1) the day falls within a period of n days dating from a given day` `the day my period dates from` `the day I am asking about` `the number of days in my period`

-- s 36(3). "If in any Act or instrument a period of time is prescribed or allowed for the doing of any thing and a power is conferred on any person or body to extend the period of time ... that power may be exercised, and ... such an application may be made, after the period of time has expired."
@export Can I still apply for an extension after my period has run out (s 36(3))?
GIVEN `my period of time is prescribed or allowed for the doing of a thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an Act or instrument give you a period of time for doing the thing?
      `a person or body has power to extend that period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Act or instrument give someone power to extend the period?
      `the extension depends on an application being made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the power to extend depend on you making an application?
      `my period has already run out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your period already run out?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I still apply for an extension after my period has run out` IS
    `s 36(3)(b) the application for an extension of the period may be made after the period has expired` `my period of time is prescribed or allowed for the doing of a thing` `a person or body has power to extend that period` `the extension depends on an application being made` `my period has already run out`

-- s 76(2) and Schedule 4. Working day: not a Saturday or Sunday, and not a public holiday or bank holiday in the place the letter was addressed to. Business day: not a Saturday or Sunday, and not a public holiday or bank holiday throughout the State.
@export Is the day I am asking about a working day (s 76(2))?
GIVEN `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which day do you want to know about?
      `the public and bank holidays in the place the letter was addressed to` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc Which days are public holidays or bank holidays in the place the letter was addressed to? (list each day)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the day I am asking about a working day` IS
    `s 76(2) the day is a working day` `the day I am asking about` `the public and bank holidays in the place the letter was addressed to`

@export Is the day I am asking about a business day (Schedule 4)?
GIVEN `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which day do you want to know about?
      `the public and bank holidays throughout the State` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc Which days are public holidays or bank holidays throughout New South Wales? (list each day)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the day I am asking about a business day` IS
    `Schedule 4 the day is a business day` `the day I am asking about` `the public and bank holidays throughout the State`

§§ `When an Act or a statutory rule takes effect (sections 23 to 26, 39)`

-- s 23(1), (2) and (5). An Act commences 28 days after assent unless it provides for its commencement, or a day is appointed by proclamation under s 23(2); a proclamation published after the day appointed moves commencement to the publication day (the earlier of that day and the day the Act would have commenced otherwise).
@export On which day does the Act commence (s 23)?
GIVEN `the date of assent to the Act` IS A DATE @desc On which day did the Act receive the Royal Assent?
      `the Act itself names the day it commences` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Act itself name the day it commences, or say how to work it out?
      `the day the Act names` IS A DATE @desc If the Act names the day, which day is it? (any day if it does not)
      `a proclamation appoints the day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the day of commencement appointed by a proclamation?
      `the day the proclamation appoints` IS A DATE @desc Which day does the proclamation appoint? (any day if there is no proclamation)
      `the day the proclamation is published` IS A DATE @desc On which day is the proclamation published? (any day if there is no proclamation)
      `the Act does not provide for its own commencement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Act silent on when it commences, so that the Governor appoints the day under section 23(2)?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On which day does the Act commence` IS
    `s 23(1) and (5) the day an Act commences` `the date of assent to the Act` basis
    WHERE
        basis MEANS
            IF `the Act itself names the day it commences`
            THEN ProvidedFixedDay `the day the Act names`
            ELSE IF `a proclamation appoints the day`
                 THEN IF `the Act does not provide for its own commencement`
                      THEN AppointedUnderSubsection2 `the day the proclamation appoints` `the day the proclamation is published`
                      ELSE ProvidedProclamation `the day the proclamation appoints` `the day the proclamation is published`
                 ELSE NothingProvided

-- s 39(1)(b) and (2A). A statutory rule commences on the day it is published on the NSW legislation website or, if a later day is specified in the rule, on that later day; a rule that specifies an earlier day commences on the publication day.
@export On which day does the statutory rule commence (s 39)?
GIVEN `the day the statutory rule is published on the NSW legislation website` IS A DATE @desc On which day is the statutory rule published on the NSW legislation website?
      `the rule specifies a day for its commencement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the rule itself specify a day for it to commence?
      `the day the rule specifies` IS A DATE @desc Which day does the rule specify? (any day if it specifies none)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On which day does the statutory rule commence` IS
    `s 39(1)(b) and (2A) the day a statutory rule commences` `the day the statutory rule is published on the NSW legislation website` specified
    WHERE
        specified MEANS IF `the rule specifies a day for its commencement` THEN JUST `the day the rule specifies` ELSE NOTHING

-- s 24. An Act or statutory rule that commences on a particular day commences at the beginning of that day. Another instrument is not covered by s 24.
@export Has the Act or statutory rule commenced at the moment I am asking about (s 24)?
GIVEN `what it is` IS A TimeTextKind @desc Is it an Act, a statutory rule or another instrument? (choose AnAct, AStatutoryRule or AnotherInstrument)
      `the day it commences` IS A DATE @desc On which day does it commence?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which day do you want to know about?
      `I am asking about the end of that day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you mean the end of that day (yes) or the beginning of it (no)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the Act or statutory rule commenced at the moment I am asking about` IS
    CONSIDER `s 24 the moment an Act or statutory rule commences on a particular day` `what it is` `the day it commences`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST commenced THEN JUST (`day point is no later than day point` commenced asked)
    WHERE
        asked MEANS IF `I am asking about the end of that day` THEN EndOfDay `the day I am asking about` ELSE BeginningOfDay `the day I am asking about`

@export Is the Act or instrument still operating at the moment I am asking about (s 71)?
GIVEN `the day it is expressed to expire, lapse, cease to have effect or remain in force until` IS A DATE @desc On which day is the Act or instrument expressed to expire, lapse or cease to have effect, or to remain in force until?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which day do you want to know about?
      `I am asking about the end of that day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you mean the end of that day (yes) or the beginning of it (no)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the Act or instrument still operating at the moment I am asking about` IS
    NOT (`day point is no later than day point` (`s 71 the moment an Act or instrument expressed to expire or remain in force until a day stops operating` `the day it is expressed to expire, lapse, cease to have effect or remain in force until`) asked)
    WHERE
        asked MEANS IF `I am asking about the end of that day` THEN EndOfDay `the day I am asking about` ELSE BeginningOfDay `the day I am asking about`

@export Has the repeal taken effect at the moment I am asking about (s 30D)?
GIVEN `the day of the repeal` IS A DATE @desc On which day is the Act, instrument or provision repealed?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which day do you want to know about?
      `I am asking about the end of that day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you mean the end of that day (yes) or the beginning of it (no)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the repeal taken effect at the moment I am asking about` IS
    `day point is no later than day point` (`s 30D the moment a repeal on a day takes effect` `the day of the repeal`) asked
    WHERE
        asked MEANS IF `I am asking about the end of that day` THEN EndOfDay `the day I am asking about` ELSE BeginningOfDay `the day I am asking about`

§§ `Repeals and what continues (sections 29 and 30C)`

-- s 29. If an Act or statutory rule repeals provisions and enacts new provisions in substitution, the repealed provisions continue in force until the new provisions commence.
@export Are the repealed provisions still in force on the day I am asking about (s 29)?
GIVEN `the repeal replaces the provisions with new provisions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the repealing Act or statutory rule enact new provisions in substitution for the ones it repeals?
      `the day the new provisions commence` IS A DATE @desc On which day do the new provisions commence?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which day do you want to know about?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the repealed provisions still in force on the day I am asking about` IS
    `s 29 the repealed provisions are in force on the day` TRUE `the repeal replaces the provisions with new provisions` `the day the new provisions commence` `the day I am asking about`

-- s 30C. An amending Act enacted after 1 January 2009 is repealed on the day after all of its provisions have commenced (or the day after assent, if it commenced before assent), unless it makes provision for its own repeal.
@export On which day is the amending Act repealed (s 30C)?
GIVEN `the date of assent to the amending Act` IS A DATE @desc On which day did the amending Act receive the Royal Assent?
      `the last day on which a provision of the amending Act commences` IS A DATE @desc On which day does the last of its provisions commence?
      `the amending Act makes provision for its own repeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the amending Act itself make provision for its own repeal?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On which day is the amending Act repealed` IS
    `s 30C the day section 30C repeals the amending Act` `the date of assent to the amending Act` `the last day on which a provision of the amending Act commences` `the amending Act makes provision for its own repeal`

§§ `Statutory rules and Parliament (sections 40 and 41)`

-- s 40(4). Failure to lay the written notice before each House in accordance with section 40 does not affect the operation of a statutory rule; the notice must nevertheless be laid.
@export Does the statutory rule I rely on stop working if the written notice was not laid before Parliament in time (s 40(4))?
GIVEN `the written notice was not laid before each House of Parliament in accordance with section 40` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the written notice of the making of the rule not laid before each House of Parliament in accordance with section 40?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the statutory rule I rely on stop working if the written notice was not laid before Parliament in time` IS
    `s 40(4) the failure to lay the written notice affects the operation of the statutory rule` `the written notice was not laid before each House of Parliament in accordance with section 40`

-- s 41(1)(b) with s 18. After the written notice is laid, a House may pass a resolution disallowing the rule only if notice of the resolution was given within 15 sitting days of the House after the notice was laid. So the rule you rely on can be disallowed until the 15th sitting day after the notice was laid (a day known only from the days the House sat).
@export Until which day can notice of a motion to disallow the statutory rule I rely on still be given (s 41(1))?
GIVEN `the days the House sat` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc On which days did the House sit after the written notice was laid? (list each day)
      `the day the written notice was laid before the House` IS A DATE @desc On which day was the written notice laid before the House?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Until which day can notice of a motion to disallow the statutory rule still be given` IS
    `s 18 the nth sitting day of a House after a day` `the days the House sat` `the day the written notice was laid before the House` 15

@export Can the statutory rule I rely on still be disallowed by a resolution of a House (s 41(1))?
GIVEN `the days the House sat` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc On which days did the House sit after the written notice was laid? (list each day)
      `the written notice has been laid before the House` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the written notice of the making of the rule already been laid before the House?
      `the day the written notice was laid before the House` IS A DATE @desc On which day was the written notice laid? (any day if it has not been laid)
      `the day notice of the resolution was given` IS A DATE @desc On which day was notice of the resolution given?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the statutory rule I rely on still be disallowed` IS
    `s 41(1) either House may pass a resolution disallowing the statutory rule` `the days the House sat` laid `the day notice of the resolution was given`
    WHERE
        laid MEANS IF `the written notice has been laid before the House` THEN JUST `the day the written notice was laid before the House` ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Serving a document by post (section 76)`

-- s 76(1)(b). Service by post in Australia or an external Territory is taken to have been effected on the seventh working day after the letter was posted, unless evidence sufficient to raise doubt is adduced to the contrary. A working day is not a Saturday or Sunday, or a public holiday or bank holiday in the place the letter was addressed to.
@export On which day is the document I posted taken to have been served (s 76(1))?
GIVEN `an Act or instrument authorises or requires the document to be served by post` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an Act or instrument authorise or require the document to be served by post?
      `the letter was properly addressed, prepaid and posted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the letter properly addressed, prepaid and posted?
      `the letter was posted in Australia or in an external Territory` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the letter posted in Australia or in an external Territory?
      `evidence sufficient to raise doubt has been adduced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has evidence sufficient to raise doubt been adduced that it was not received on that day?
      `the day the letter was posted` IS A DATE @desc On which day was the letter posted?
      `the public and bank holidays in the place the letter was addressed to` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc Which days are public holidays or bank holidays in the place the letter was addressed to? (list each day)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On which day is the document I posted taken to have been served` IS
    `s 76(1)(b) the day service is taken to have been effected` `an Act or instrument authorises or requires the document to be served by post` `the letter was properly addressed, prepaid and posted` `the letter was posted in Australia or in an external Territory` `evidence sufficient to raise doubt has been adduced` `the day the letter was posted` `the public and bank holidays in the place the letter was addressed to`

§§ `Forms (section 80)`

-- s 80(1). If a form is prescribed by, or approved under, an Act or statutory rule, strict compliance with the form is not necessary but substantial compliance is sufficient.
@export Is it enough that I substantially followed the form (s 80(1))?
GIVEN `a form is prescribed by, or approved under, an Act or statutory rule` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the form prescribed by, or approved under, an Act or statutory rule?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it enough that I substantially followed the form` IS
    `s 80(1) substantial compliance with the form is sufficient` `a form is prescribed by, or approved under, an Act or statutory rule`

§§ `Age and minors (section 37 and Schedule 4)`

-- s 37. A person attains an age in years at the beginning of the person's birthday for that age. A person born on 29 February has no birthday in a year that is not a leap year, and the Act does not say what happens.
@export On which day does the person attain the age (s 37)?
GIVEN `the person's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is the person's date of birth?
      `the age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc Which age, in whole years, do you want to know about?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On which day does the person attain the age` IS
    CONSIDER `s 37 the moment a person attains an age in years` `the person's date of birth` `the age in years`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST (BeginningOfDay d) THEN JUST d
    WHEN JUST (EndOfDay d) THEN JUST d

@export Is the person a minor at the moment I am asking about (s 37, Schedule 4)?
GIVEN `the person is a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a natural person (not a company)?
      `the person's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is the person's date of birth?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which day do you want to know about?
      `I am asking about the end of that day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you mean the end of that day (yes) or the beginning of it (no)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the person a minor at the moment I am asking about` IS
    `Schedule 4 the person is a minor at the moment` `the person is a natural person` `the person's date of birth` asked
    WHERE
        asked MEANS IF `I am asking about the end of that day` THEN EndOfDay `the day I am asking about` ELSE BeginningOfDay `the day I am asking about`

§§ `Measuring a distance (section 38)`

-- s 38. Under an Act passed before the commencement of the Interpretation Act 1987, or an instrument made under such an Act, a distance is measured along the nearest route ordinarily used in travelling; under an Act passed after it, or an instrument made under such an Act, in a straight line on a horizontal plane.
@export How is the distance measured (s 38)?
GIVEN `the distance is measured for the purposes of` IS A PurposeOfMeasuringDistance @desc Is the distance measured for an Act passed before the Interpretation Act 1987 commenced, for an instrument made under such an Act, for an Act passed after it commenced, or for an instrument made under such an Act? (choose AnActPassedBeforeTheCommencementOfThisAct, AnInstrumentMadeUnderAnActPassedBeforeTheCommencementOfThisAct, AnActPassedAfterTheCommencementOfThisAct, AnInstrumentMadeUnderAnActPassedAfterTheCommencementOfThisAct or SomeOtherPurposeOfMeasuringDistance)
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
DECIDE `How is the distance measured` IS
    CONSIDER `s 38 the way the distance is measured` `the distance is measured for the purposes of`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST AlongTheNearestRouteOrdinarilyUsedInTravelling THEN JUST "along the nearest route ordinarily used in travelling"
    WHEN JUST InAStraightLineOnAHorizontalPlane THEN JUST "in a straight line on a horizontal plane"
